    "contact": "Linden Department of Public Works, 908-474-8666",
    "notes": [
        "Put carts behind the curb with the lids closed by 6:00 AM on your collection day, and take the empty carts in by 6:00 AM the next day. Keep them at least 3 feet from poles, signs, cars, trees and other carts. Items left next to a cart are not collected.",
        "Green cart: household garbage. Blue cart: glass and plastic bottles and jugs, aluminum and tin cans, empty aerosol cans. Brown cart: newspapers, junk mail, magazines, school and computer paper, wrapping paper, delivery boxes, cardboard, cereal and snack boxes, books without hard covers. Never put recyclables in plastic bags. Packing material, tape, plastic bags and Styrofoam go in the garbage. One extra cart of each color can be rented for $60.",
        "Bulk Trash & Yard Waste day comes four times a year: household trash, bulk items, furniture, appliances, yard waste and fully dried latex paint. Cut wood and metal pipes into 4-foot lengths, roll and tie carpet in 4-foot lengths, tie branches and brush with rope or twine, drain fuel and oil from lawn equipment, take rims off car tires (no truck tires). Mattresses and box springs must be wrapped in plastic. Not taken: asphalt, bricks, cinder blocks, concrete, patio block, chemicals, propane tanks, oils and oil-based paint.",
        "Each home also gets one special trash removal a year; more cost $150 each. Call the DPW to arrange it.",
        "Grass: mower clippings only, in biodegradable paper bags or open 32-gallon cans. Bagged leaves go out the same way. Never put grass, yard waste, branches or bushes in the street.",
        "From October 1 to December 11 loose leaves may be raked into the curb line (no dirt, rocks or sticks, at least 10 feet from storm drains). They are collected district by district as weather allows, so there are no set days.",
        "Drop-off at Public Works, 700 Lower Rd: household trash only, Monday to Saturday 8 AM to 2 PM, once a week, proof of Linden residency required, no contractors.",
        "Recycling Center, 2 Donaldson Pl (off W Elizabeth Ave), Monday to Friday 7 AM to 2:30 PM, Saturday 8 AM to 2 PM, proof of residency required: all recyclables, appliances (doors removed), metals, TVs and computers, motor and cooking oil, paper-bagged leaves (October to April) and grass (April to October). Ten free paper leaf bags in November and December.",
        "On a holiday the DPW is closed. Pickups that week can move a day earlier or a day later, and it differs by district; this website shows the day from your district's calendar. Extreme weather may delay or cancel collection.",
        "Recycling is the law: recyclables found in the garbage get a warning, and repeat offenders a summons with fines of up to $250."
    ],
    "sources": [
        "2026 district collection calendars (City of Linden DPW, \"DISTRICT 1 - Collection Schedule 2026\" to 10, spreadsheets), checked 2026-11-19, linked as \"2026 Garbage Disposal Schedules\" from https://linden-nj.gov/directory/recycling/ (Google Drive folder https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cKHVvy9Ub6beM-l2l6SwKeiXTGmPS94r). Every date is in data/reference/linden_2026_calendar.json, made with tools/linden_calendar.py.",
        "2026 Solid Waste Collection Calendar and Service Guide, \"2026 OUTER INSTRUCTIONS - All DISTRICTS\" (same folder), checked 2026-11-19: notes and contact.",
        "Recycling page, https://linden-nj.gov/directory/recycling/, checked 2026-11-19: recycling fines.",
        "DPW Residential Solid Waste Collection Districts map (July 2020), https://linden-nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/DPW-Collection-District.pdf: the districts. They are not the city's wards."
    ]
